// Login endpoint hands the raw JWT back in the response body.
// The SPA then does localStorage.setItem("jwt", token) — readable by ANY script.
@PostMapping("/auth/login")
public ResponseEntity<Map<String, String>> login(@RequestBody LoginRequest req) {
    var user = authService.authenticate(req.username(), req.password());
    var token = jwtUtil.generateToken(user.getUsername());
    // Token travels in JSON; client must store it in JS-accessible storage.
    return ResponseEntity.ok(Map.of("token", token)); // XSS can steal this
}
```
Any injected script can read `localStorage` and exfiltrate the token.

